	(text "12 V fan switched by 3.3 V logic - a gate booster built from my own parts"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40 26 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.0 3.0)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "63bb1978-1533-4be3-bc5a-7a2cbef79e1c")
	)
	(text "Arduino Pro Mini (3.3 V) pin D9 = OC1A.  Q2 (2N7002) pulls the IRF7416 gate low; the IRF7416 then drives the IRFZ44N gate from +12 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40 34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.7 1.7)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1ee4c682-2f12-4836-a20d-bab844f39dc0")
	)
	(text "WHY THREE TRANSISTORS\nThe bins hold 12x IRFZ44N, 11x 2N7002 and 6x IRF7416, and no logic-level N-channel\nthat can carry a 12 V / 100 mA fan:\n- 2N7002: Id max 115 mA in my own spec record, and at Vgs = 3.0 V it only conducts\n  52 mA.  As the pass element it starves the fan and burns 300 mW, over its 200 mW\n  rating.  Here it is only a level shifter, never the pass transistor.\n- IRFZ44N: Rds(on) is specified only at Vgs = 10 V, and Vgs(th) is guaranteed\n  2.0 V .. 4.0 V.  Wired straight to the pin, /GATE only reaches 3.0 V (R1/R5\n  divider): a typical unit runs the fan but wastes 5.2 mW, and a worst-case unit\n  (Vgs(th) = 4.0 V) never turns on at all.  sim/variants.py measures every case.\nSo the 3.3 V pin only drives small signals; the +12 V rail does the real gate drive."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40 44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "74629112-06ab-4df2-b8bb-46c856a33612")
	)
	(text "HOW IT WORKS\n1. Pin low: Q2 is off, no current flows in R3, so /BOOT is pulled to +12 V.  Q3 (source\n   on +12 V) sees Vgs = 0 and stays off; R5 holds /GATE at 0 V.  The fan is off.\n2. Pin high: R1/R2 give Q2's gate 3.0 V, Q2 turns on and sinks 12 V / 10 k = 1.2 mA, so\n   /BOOT collapses to 12 mV.  Q3 now sees Vgs = -12 V and turns on hard.\n3. +12 V reaches Q1's gate through R4; R4 and R5 form a divider, so /GATE settles at\n   12 V x 10 k / 11 k = 10.9 V - the region where the datasheet quotes 17.5 mOhm.\n4. Q1 is fully enhanced: Rds(on) 16 mOhm, V(drain) 1.6 mV, 0.16 mW lost, and the fan\n   gets the whole 12 V.  The Arduino pin itself never sources more than 0.3 mA.\n5. The logic is not inverted, and at power-up the pin is floating: R2 keeps Q2 off, so\n   Q3 is off, so Q1 is off.  The fan cannot drift on.\n6. Q3's SOURCE must be the +12 V side.  Swap source and drain and the P-FET's body\n   diode feeds +12 V into Q1's gate, and the fan can never switch off.\n7. D1 (1N5819, cathode to +12 V) catches the fan winding's current when Q1 opens:\n   /DRAIN peaks at 12.37 V instead of spiking hundreds of volts.\n8. C1 and C2 are not purchased parts: they are the two MOSFETs' own input capacitances\n   (Ciss) drawn explicitly so the gate RC time constants are visible.  L1 + R6 are a\n   model of the fan - the bins hold no 12 V fan."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 196 44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6459f14a-cb81-46ff-b395-32d3cf2eefc4")
	)
	(text "MEASURED BY sim/run.sh (ngspice)\nfan starts conducting at 2.27 V on the pin        /GATE settles at 10.91 V\nfan current 102 mA, V(drain) 1.6 mV               Rds(on) 15.7 mOhm -> 0.16 mW in Q1\nturn-off spike clamped to 12.37 V                 pin current never above 0.30 mA\n/GATE rise 5 tau = 7.5 us (R4 x C1)               /BOOT rise 5 tau = 85 us (R3 x C2)\nfan L/R = 83 us, so at 1 kHz it is chopped 0..100 mA; average at 50 % duty = 54 mA"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40 74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4e925467-1793-4e5b-a36c-dccd43c6a6d0")
	)
	(text "TRY IT YOURSELF   (Simulator > Run Simulator, then Transient or DC Sweep)\n- Run the DC sweep: /BOOT falls from 12 V to 0.01 V while /GATE jumps from 0 to 10.9 V.\n- Delete Q2, Q3, R3, R4 and C2 and wire R1 straight to /GATE: the fan still runs (100 mA),\n  but Q1 now burns 5.2 mW instead of 0.16 mW.  Then swap in irfz44n_wc.lib: fan stops dead.\n- Shorten R3 to 1 k and watch the turn-off delay shrink from ~55 us to a few us.\n- Remove D1 and look at the /DRAIN spike at turn-off: that is what the diode absorbs.\n- Change V2's PULSE width tw from 500u to 250u (25 % duty): average fan current falls,\n  the pulses the fan sees stay a full 12 V.  Speed control without dimming the motor."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40 222 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0ab43fa1-ccc5-4734-942e-ad6919014b91")
	)
	(text "PARTS - all from my cabinets\nU1  Arduino Pro Mini 3V3       L1 - C5   x1  (on three female sockets)\nQ1  IRFZ44N   TO-220           R1 - B4   x12\nQ2  2N7002    SOT-23           R1 - A4   x11\nQ3  IRF7416   SO-8             R1 - A4   x6  (a breakout board in the same drawer)\nD1  1N5819    40 V 1 A Schottky L1 - E1  x30\nD2  1N5822    40 V 3 A DO-27   L1 - E1   x9   spare, not soldered\nD3  MBR10100CT 10 A dual       L1 - E1   x3   spare, not soldered\nQ4  BC547     TO-92            R1 - D3   x20\nR1, R4    1 k                 R1 - A2   x20\nR2, R3, R5   10 k             R1 - B2   x20\nV1  12 V supply module         L1 - B7   x2\nC1, C2, L1, R6 are model artefacts, not bin parts"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 155 222 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "01871b9b-dc16-496b-a455-2258a725de72")
	)
	(text "PHYSICAL PINOUTS - symbols use package pin order: sheet numbers = board legs\nQ2  2N7002  SOT-23    1 gate /LGATE    2 source /GND     3 drain /BOOT\nQ3  IRF7416 SO-8      1,2,3 source /P12V   4 gate /BOOT   5..8 drain /HIGATE\nQ1  IRFZ44N TO-220    1 gate /GATE     2 drain /DRAIN    3 source /GND\nQ4  BC547   TO-92     1 emitter /GND   2 base /TBASE     3 collector /NUC_TACH\nD1  1N5819  DO-41     banded end (cathode) to +12 V, other end to /DRAIN\nJ3  3 fans            odd pins = +12 V, even pins = the switched /DRAIN side\nngspice's own order (D-G-S-B, C-B-E) lives in the sim/models/ subckt wrappers\nJ5  FTDI    1 DTR  2 TX0  3 RX1  4 P3V3  5 GND  6 BLK\nJ6  ICSP    1 MISO 3 SCK  4 MOSI 5 RST  6 GND   (pin 2 stays dead)\nU1  35 module holes: symbol pin number = socket pad number\ndocs/pcb-notes.md carries the full pad-to-net table for the board."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 155 250 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6c1e0f6a-2f57-4f8e-9a1b-0d5c3b7e4a11")
	)
	(text "* Simulation setup: KiCad hands these lines straight to ngspice.\n* DC sweep of the pin drive 0 -> 3.3 V, then 1 kHz PWM (50 %) for 5 ms.\n.op\n.dc V2 0 3.3 0.01\n.tran 1u 5m\n.print dc v(/BOOT) v(/GATE) v(/DRAIN) i(v1) i(v2)\n.print tran v(/GATE) v(/DRAIN) i(l1) i(v2)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40 248 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e9c551b4-b894-492e-b8c5-86215f15cbd6")
	)
	(text "1. level shifter"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101 214 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
